  "title": "Editing or Deleting a Cloud Storage Integration",
  "source": {
    "url": "https://help.zscaler.com/zpc/editing-or-deleting-cloud-storage-integration",
    "node": "1395686",
    "revision": "2750506",
    "updated": "2026-01-06",
    "updated_basis": "pdf-last-modified"
  },
  "captured_at": "2026-11-04",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "text": "You can edit or delete any cloud storage integration (Amazon S3 Bucket, Azure Blob Storage, or Amazon Security Lake) as required."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Editing a Cloud Storage Integration",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "To edit a cloud storage integration:"
    },
    {
      "item": "Go to Administration > Integrations.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          20
        ],
        [
          23,
          35
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "On the Integrations page, click the Edit icon for the cloud storage that you want to edit.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          19
        ],
        [
          36,
          40
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "In the Edit Integration window:",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 3,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          23
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "For Amazon S3 Bucket integration, change the Integration Name, Amazon S3 Bucket Name, or Folder Location.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          45,
          61
        ],
        [
          63,
          84
        ],
        [
          89,
          104
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Whenever you edit an Amazon S3 Bucket integration, you must test the connection again.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "For Azure Blob Storage integration, change the Integration Name, Azure Storage Connection String, or Folder Location.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          47,
          63
        ],
        [
          65,
          96
        ],
        [
          101,
          116
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "For Amazon Security Lake, change the Integration Name, IAM Role, Amazon S3 Bucket Name, Folder Location, and Bucket Region as required.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          37,
          53
        ],
        [
          55,
          63
        ],
        [
          65,
          86
        ],
        [
          88,
          103
        ],
        [
          109,
          122
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "If you change the Amazon S3 Bucket Name or Folder Location, you must test the connection again.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          18,
          39
        ],
        [
          43,
          58
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Save.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 4,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Deleting a Cloud Storage Integration",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "To delete a cloud storage integration:"
    },
    {
      "item": "Go to Administration > Integrations.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          20
        ],
        [
          23,
          35
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "On the Integrations page, click the Delete icon for the cloud storage that you want to delete.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          19
        ],
        [
          36,
          42
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "In the Delete Integration window, read the message related to alert rules.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 3,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          25
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "You cannot delete an integration if it is associated with alert rules. You must first move the alert rules to another integration. Until then, the Delete button is disabled.",
      "depth": 0,
      "strong": [
        [
          147,
          153
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "After you've moved the alert rules, click Delete to delete the integration.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 4,
      "strong": [
        [
          42,
          48
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
}
